file_name": "PasiphaeVR_5.png", "id": "1569596694176219", "uri": "https://scontent-sjc6-1.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/491824322_1569596700842885_2180200080814841656_n.png?_nc_cat=101&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=Wkc-iXLTtOUQ7kNvwHaaSGu&_nc_oc=AdrmASAva4fJiLbydS8Da0cKrRdnuh-_gohaChkTcW3p-UqM8mKKG0eqgMfl-tr_L34&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-sjc6-1.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQSx97gbRGLf0MJQ_4Elei9-9D3taGM5sg3a-dZqJhObyw&oe=6B0330C6"}], "video_trailer": null, "video_trailer_thumbnail": {"file_name": "Frame-00060.png", "id": "2883980735278412", "uri": "https://scontent-sjc3-1.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/491820887_2883980738611745_7070582803337495383_n.png?_nc_cat=106&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=Mfs0Yb3JUboQ7kNvwHLnRr4&_nc_oc=Adqqf8uOOemaNaQ7BPhi-Yt6MyQwFvAyX8FenMQUShGNnqTzMjc6QELiZQD4bA6T3-c&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-sjc3-1.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQSNbHHuMSTmM92FrW8PoO9syKPdZ5dZQvmXO9Kr2Lxg_w&oe=6B0304A5"}, "display_name": "PasiphaeVR Prototype", "keywords": [], "long_description": "Step inside our Galaxy.\n\nThis VR experience combines the Gaia star map with measurements from PASIPHAE, a project that studies the faint \u201cpolarization\u201d of starlight\u2014a subtle signature imprinted as light travels through cosmic dust. That dust is gently guided by the Milky Way\u2019s large-scale magnetic field, so the pattern in the light helps us trace how magnetism is arranged in the space between the stars.\n\nIn the app you can:\n - Fly through a 3D view of the Milky Way built from ~140 million Gaia stars,\n - See direction markers on selected stars that show how their light was affected on its journey to us,\n - Explore different reconstructions of dust clouds, plus an all-sky dust map for context.\n\nIt\u2019s real astronomy data, turned into a place you can explore, revealing the otherwise invisible structure of dust and magnetism that shapes our Galaxy.\n\nThe PASIPHAE experiment has been funded by the 